WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.920
A traditional mirror operates on strict
physical law.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.520
It provides a one-to-one synchronization
between your body and its

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.000
reflection, proving your presence.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.040
We have learned to process static
deepfakes by looking for

5
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.040
the seams. Because they are pre-recorded,
the brain categorizes them

6
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.640
as external media, a digital object
separate from our own

7
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.840
current state. This raises a question for
the era of

8
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.080
generative AI. What happens when that
one-to-one physical response is

9
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.480
merged with synthetic manipulation?

10
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.000
When these two systems collide, the result
is a vacuum.

11
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.600
The brain struggles to reconcile the
real-time movement it expects

12
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.920
with the artificial image it sees.

13
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.480
Latent Self is an interactive, real-time
face-morphing installation.

14
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.440
It is designed as a physical kiosk
mimicking the presence

15
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.600
of a standard mirror within a gallery.

16
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.920
When you stand in front of it, the
reflection is

17
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.840
instantly recognizable as you.

18
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.960
It mimics your movements with low latency,
yet the features

19
00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.480
of your face are shifted.

20
00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.280
The system allows you to adjust your
reflection along specific

21
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.680
paths, such as age, gender, and species,
or change the

22
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.440
intensity of a smile.

23
00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.360
Because you control these specific shifts,
you are a participant

24
00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:13.800
in the distortion.

25
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.720
The installation moves the focus from the
technology itself to

26
00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.880
the feeling of seeing your identity
manipulated in real time.

27
00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.880
The engine behind the screen is Style
GAN2ADA.

28
00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.920
Unlike a simple filter that pastes an
image over your

29
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.240
face, this architecture works by
recalculating your appearance from the

30
00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.160
inside out. This is a representation of
latent space.

31
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.080
It is a multi-dimensional mathematical map
where the AI has

32
00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.240
organized every possible human facial
feature into a system of

33
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.240
coordinates. When the kiosk scans your
face, it plots your

34
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:53.560
specific biology as a single numeric
coordinate within this map.

35
00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.000
This point is your origin.

36
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.400
It is the mathematical definition of how
you look at

37
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.560
the moment you step in front of the
mirror.

38
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.240
By turning your face into a coordinate,
the system removes

39
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.560
biological limits. Your identity becomes a
location on a map

40
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.920
that can be moved.

41
00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.520
When selecting an option like age, you
aren't just applying

42
00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.720
a mask. You're telling the AI to find the
direction

43
00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.960
on the map representing older.

44
00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.560
To create the change, the AI calculates a
trajectory from

45
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.480
your origin point along a specific
mathematical vector.

46
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.840
As you move or breathe, your origin point
shifts.

47
00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.920
The system recalculates the vector
instantly, ensuring the morph stays

48
00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.720
attached to your real-time
microexpressions.

49
00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.160
The speed of these calculations allows the
software to recede

50
00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.360
into the background.

51
00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.480
You are left with a reflection that feels
alive, even

52
00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.560
as it ceases to be accurate.

53
00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.000
This creates a very specific kind of
cognitive dissonance.

54
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.720
Because the image responds to your
smallest movements, your brain

55
00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:57.160
cannot easily dismiss the reflection as a
pre-rendered fake.

56
00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.200
This places the viewer in the uncanny gap.

57
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.280
You are suspended between recognizing
yourself and feeling a sense

58
00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.920
of estrangement from the face in the
mirror.

59
00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.920
The installation hides its technical
complexity to ensure you stay

60
00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.600
focused on this feeling.

61
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.560
Without visible interface distractions,
the dissonance remains front and center.

62
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.640
This discomfort has a purpose.

63
00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.000
It forces the viewer to examine how they
recognize themselves

64
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.880
when their physical features are no longer
constant.

65
00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:29.320
The installation moves away from the
binary of real versus

66
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:33.720
fake imagery. It occupies a space where
those categories overlap.

67
00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:37.480
By moving your identity along a
mathematical axis, the mirror

68
00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.360
shows a version of you derived from
probability.

69
00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.560
It is a reflection of a plausible
alternate state.

70
00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.600
Since mirrors have always been our primary
tool for self-verification,

71
00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.440
introducing these latent vectors changes
the nature of the reflection.

72
00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.160
In this context, the mirror does more than
confirm your

73
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.760
current appearance, it presents the
unsettling reality of who you

74
00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:58.960
almost are.

